# Deployment Rule

## Branch Naming

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Feature | `feat/[TICKET-ID]-short-description` | `feat/PROJ-123-user-login` |
| Bug fix | `fix/[TICKET-ID]-short-description` | `fix/PROJ-456-null-token-crash` |
| Hotfix | `hotfix/[TICKET-ID]-short-description` | `hotfix/PROJ-789-prod-auth-failure` |
| Chore | `chore/[TICKET-ID]-short-description` | `chore/PROJ-100-upgrade-react-19` |
| Docs | `docs/short-description` | `docs/update-api-guide` |

## Commit Message Format

Follow Conventional Commits specification:
```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body>

<footer>
```

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `chore`, `hotfix`

**Subject:** imperative mood, max 72 chars, no period at end

**Body (required for non-trivial changes):**
- What changed and why
- Max 100 chars per line

**Footer (required):**
```
Implements: PROJ-123
Resolves: PROJ-123
Acceptance: PROJ-123-AC-1, PROJ-123-AC-2, PROJ-123-AC-3
Tests: auth.test.ts:[PROJ-123-AC-1], auth.test.ts:[PROJ-123-AC-2]
Breaking-Change: [describe if applicable]
```

The `Acceptance:` footer lists every AC this commit addresses.
The `Tests:` footer lists the test files and their embedded AC IDs.

**Examples:**
```
feat(auth): add JWT refresh token rotation

Refresh tokens are now single-use. On each refresh, a new
refresh token is issued and the old one invalidated.

Implements: PROJ-123
Acceptance: PROJ-123-AC-1, PROJ-123-AC-2, PROJ-123-AC-3
Tests: auth.service.test.ts:[PROJ-123-AC-1][PROJ-123-AC-2][PROJ-123-AC-3]
```

```
fix(cart): prevent negative quantities on item update

Guard clause added before updating cart item quantity.
Previously, POST /cart/items with qty=-1 silently corrupted state.

Resolves: PROJ-456
Acceptance: PROJ-456-AC-1
Tests: cart.test.ts:[PROJ-456-AC-1]
```

## Pull Request Standards

### PR Title
Same as commit subject: `type(scope): description`

### PR Body Template
```markdown
## Summary
<!-- 1-3 bullet points describing what this PR does -->

## Ticket
Implements: [TICKET-ID](link)

## AC Traceability
| AC ID | Summary | Test | Status |
|-------|---------|------|--------|
| [TICKET-ID]-AC-1 | [summary] | [file:test-name] | ✅ |
| [TICKET-ID]-AC-2 | [summary] | [file:test-name] | ✅ |

## Changes
- `path/to/file.ts`: description of change
- `path/to/other.ts`: description of change

## Test Plan
- [ ] All ACs have at least one test (see table above)
- [ ] Unit tests added: `npm test src/auth/`
- [ ] Integration tests pass: `npm test`
- [ ] Manually verified: [describe steps]
- [ ] Edge cases covered: [list]

## Screenshots (if UI change)

## Checklist
- [ ] Tests pass locally
- [ ] AC Traceability Matrix complete (no ❌ rows)
- [ ] No linting errors
- [ ] No type errors
- [ ] Docs updated (if needed)
- [ ] No secrets in code
```

### PR Size
- Target: < 400 lines changed
- If larger, split into a stacked PR series
- Each PR should represent one logical change

## Release Checklist

Before merging to main/master:
- [ ] All CI checks pass (tests, lint, type-check, security scan)
- [ ] At least one human reviewer approved (if team project)
- [ ] No merge conflicts
- [ ] Release notes / CHANGELOG updated
- [ ] Version bumped if applicable (semver)

## Post-Merge
- Tag the release if applicable: `git tag -a v1.2.3 -m "Release v1.2.3"`
- Update Jira ticket status to "In Review" → "Done"
- Notify stakeholders if user-facing change
